4.4 Modifying Strings
=====================

You can alter the contents of a mutable string via operations described
in this section.  *Note Mutability::.

   The most basic way to alter the contents of an existing string is
with ‘aset’ (*note Array Functions::).  ‘(aset STRING IDX CHAR)’ stores
CHAR into STRING at character index IDX.  It will automatically convert
a pure-ASCII STRING to a multibyte string (*note Text Representations::)
if needed, but we recommend to always make sure STRING is multibyte
(e.g., by using ‘string-to-multibyte’, *note Converting
Representations::), if CHAR is a non-ASCII character, not a raw byte.

   To clear out a string that contained a password, use ‘clear-string’:

 -- Function: clear-string string
     This makes STRING a unibyte string and clears its contents to null
     characters.  It may also change STRING’s length.


