E.6 C Dialect
=============

The C part of Emacs is portable to C99 or later: later C features such
as ‘<stdckdint.h>’ and ‘[[noreturn]]’ are not used without a check,
typically at configuration time, and the Emacs build procedure provides
a substitute implementation if necessary.  Some later features, such as
anonymous structures and unions, are too difficult to emulate, so they
are avoided entirely.

   At some point in the future the base C dialect will no doubt change
to something later than C99.


